# [RPP](../wg/rpp.html)

## Summary

The RESTful Provisioning Protocol (RPP) Working Group met at IETF 127 in San Francisco. The session was chaired by Gavin Brown, with Andy Newton stepping in as co-chair for Marco Davenport and Charlie Lewis. 

The meeting covered working group deliverables and milestones, a major overview of core specifications updates, a proposed structural reorganization of RPP drafts, details on message handling, Internationalized Domain Name (IDN) support, the RPP extension framework, and key findings from the IETF 127 Hackathon.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### Working Group Deliverables & Milestones
- **Chairs Presentation**: [Chair slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rpp-chair-slides-00) (Gavin Brown)
- **Discussion**:
  - Gavin Brown noted that the working group hit one milestone but missed another, proposing adding six months to remaining unachieved milestones.
  - Paweł Kowalik noted that `draft-ietf-rpp-requirements` and architecture concepts remain stable. The architecture document is parked as a working group document that will be maintained, updated if necessary, and considered for publication as an Informational RFC once protocol specifications are finalized.
  - Gavin Brown emphasized keeping milestone-related documents active with regular updates and version bumps.

