### Internationalized Domain Names (IDN) in RPP
- **Presentation**: [IDN in RPP](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rpp-idn-in-rpp-03) (Martin)
- **Overview**:
  - Discussed introducing IDN handling into RPP data objects and endpoints based on Label Generation Rulesets (LGR) maintained by IANA.
  - Proposed using A-labels exclusively for URL paths and headers to avoid percent-encoding complexities, while supplying U-labels (`uName`) and LGR identifiers in JSON payloads for object creation.
- **Discussion**:
  - Paweł Kowalik supported keeping path/endpoint references strictly A-label based to maintain protocol simplicity.
  - Jim Gould cautioned that full IDN variant support is extremely complex and recommended decoupling IDN/variant specifications from the core RPP deliverables into separate extension drafts.
  - Jim Galvin summarized ongoing work in REGEXT regarding IDN variants and "same entity sets" (including diacritics and CC-TLD considerations like emojis). He recommended decoupling registry policy and language tags from strict LGR identifiers and ensuring close alignment between RPP and REGEXT work.
  - Gavin Brown cautioned against relying too heavily on IANA LGR structure naming or hardcoding LGR identifiers in object schemas, noting that language tags are less prone to breaking changes than evolving LGR tables.

