### Extending RPP
- **Presentation**: [Extending RPP](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rpp-extending-rpp-02) (Martin)
- **Overview**:
  - Extensions in RPP are additive-only and must be independent, discoverable, and non-restrictive to core features.
  - Introduced an extension guidelines document containing extension point hierarchies, standardized templates, and JSON Schema composition rules using `allOf` and `rpp:extends`.
- **Discussion**:
  - Deep asked about alignment with the JSON Schema working group efforts; Martin confirmed RPP tracks the draft specifications and relies on stable JSON Schema drafts (e.g., draft 2020-12).
  - Jim Gould and Paweł Kowalik discussed whether base data objects should formally be built using the extension mechanism ("eating your own dog food"). Paweł noted that while conceptually similar, base objects are core, but extension rules will follow the exact same structural patterns.

